", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e79186dfcf8b4bc4fb8c9d19769c9e60bbda8b6f5cd66cd0033608562e8e2997","event_uuid":"26259122-3a5c-4401-a079-71d5b85c5c9a","position":{"commit_sha":"925ef04162d21928cf7368fd0a1a5adf67a31145","position":"1787555232849128421-26259122-3a5c-4401-a079-71d5b85c5c9a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"00b9994ca7f5279e792627218306d7d8be3c433b6f8c167a7b25d23339f2ac9a","event_uuid":"df0db9fd-445b-47b2-9b49-0aee0512c128","position":{"commit_sha":"b1725f2394506b08ffd5a07df0525fa4ef68fdf2","position":"1787556868256942001-df0db9fd-445b-47b2-9b49-0aee0512c128"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"71b47d89064ec53daf7afe154753003c6db51ab983c33bd59726b31378bee33a","event_uuid":"75de2f27-983a-44fe-a393-984e187e76cb","position":{"commit_sha":"9afe3529ba8b6cc1e5a238ac4285e6064c45c70e","position":"1787556885940295001-75de2f27-983a-44fe-a393-984e187e76cb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"cd1b96f723b448920290e7957c51b7778bf22f00b693353a04eef60ebfde9e6a","event_uuid":"e36cc887-23e0-4eb7-ba6f-46550795c4d9","position":{"commit_sha":"29ecf784229076bb3c2696764c4cce4f1711184d","position":"1787556889683907001-e36cc887-23e0-4eb7-ba6f-46550795c4d9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"b51809b5c6b9b0d366d3dd4d0c6220d339b1b4019686cb351c558c7c5828248f","event_uuid":"e05de1f7-ec56-469a-8b03-cf24ee142862","position":{"commit_sha":"48bb80bb6fe85a3604365c76e55fbbc4879afaca","position":"1787558415679846001-e05de1f7-ec56-469a-8b03-cf24ee142862"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"plan_defect","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (Phase 1, proven at runtime).\n\nMechanism confirmed by reproduction in a --filter=blob:none clone whose origin.fetch maps all heads (+refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*), with a small 'main' and a large unrelated 'tickets' branch:\n\n  rebar._snapshot.repo_snapshot.resolve_ref('origin/main', ..., blobless=False) issued exactly:\n    git -c http.lowSpeedLimit=1000 -c http.lowSpeedTime=10 fetch --quiet --no-filter origin\n  i.e. NO refspec -> git applies the configured origin.fetch and transfers EVERY head. After the call, origin/tickets (the large unrelated branch, never requested) was present locally. This is the broad-fetch that made a post-merge review-plan spend 512s and time out git fetch at 300s while only a code SHA was needed.\n\nRoot cause: resolve_ref()'s FIRST fetch (repo_snapshot.py line ~265) calls fetch_origin() with no ref, so the network fetch is unscoped. fetch_origin already supports a targeted ref; only the caller was unscoped. The targeted fallback (line ~270) fires only when the broad fetch fails to resolve, so in the common origin/main case the broad fetch always runs first.\n\nDefect origin (caused_by): story hoot-glove-foyer (6d56-8c12-9953-4d25), 'Faithful, lock-free snapshot materialization core' (shipped in b25fafc, epic raze-vet-ditch). Its plan specified 'Coalesced git fetch origin ... resolve ref' — the broad, unscoped fetch by design. Hence class plan_defect: latent since introduction, surfaced under partial/promisor clone + a huge tickets branch. Distinct from strained-bare-turnstone (transport stalls / voting) and grassy-cracked-morpho (completion close scanning).\n\nFix (Phase 2): scope resolve_ref's first fetch to the requested ref — for a <remote>/<name> ref fetch '+<name>:refs/remotes/<remote>/<name>' (updates the tracking ref, transfers only that branch); otherwise pass the ref as a targeted want. Preserve blobless policy, remote-ref support, and fail-closed semantics; keep the SHA-want fallback. RED regression test pins the scoped fetch argv and rejects an unscoped no-filter origin fetch.","timestamp":1787552066225736001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 2 fix landed on branch (pre-push). Summary + before/after evidence.\n\nChange (2 src files + 1 test):\n- src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py: new _scoped_fetch_target(ref, remote) and resolve_ref now SCOPES its opening fetch to the requested ref. A remote-qualified ref (origin/main) -> forced tracking refspec '+<name>:refs/remotes/<remote>/<name>' (transfers only that branch, updates the tracking ref so rev_parse resolves); any other ref (bare SHA / plain name) -> targeted want. The SHA-want fallback is retained.\n- Fail-closed preserved: a transport/auth/stall/timeout fetch failure is remembered and re-raised (so credential/stall errors still surface with their remedy); only a genuine 'remote lacks this ref' (git_fetch.is_missing_ref) degrades to the descriptive SnapshotRefError, matching pre-fix behavior (materialize_tickets' origin/<ref> -> local fallback still works).\n- src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py: SnapshotFetchError now carries .stderr; added is_missing_ref() predicate.\n- tests/unit/test_snapshot_targeted_fetch.py: RED->GREEN regression pinning the scoped fetch argv, tracking-ref update, fail-closed on a missing ref, and SHA scoping — in a blob:none clone with a large unrelated 'tickets' branch.\n\nFetch-boundary evidence (blob:none clone, origin.fetch=+refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*, tiny main + large unrelated tickets branch, tracking refs deleted to force a real fetch):\n  BEFORE: resolve_ref('origin/main') -> git ... fetch --quiet --no-filter origin   (NO refspec) => applied all-heads refspec, CREATED refs/remotes/origin/tickets and transferred the unrelated tickets history (the 512s / 300s-timeout / ~153.6MB partial pack seen in the field).\n  AFTER:  resolve_ref('origin/main') -> git ... fetch --quiet --no-filter origin --end-of-options +main:refs/remotes/origin/main   (scoped) => refs/remotes/origin/tickets ABSENT; the tickets-only blobs remain missing (regression test asserts >= 60 unique tickets blobs unfetched). origin/main still resolves via its tracking ref.\n\nGates (worktree venv): make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS (mypy 645 files); targeted suites PASS (test_snapshot_targeted_fetch + test_repo_snapshot + blobless_747f + snapshot_cache + stall_abort_12e4 + network_fetch_851e = 50 passed; broader -k 'snapshot or fetch or resolve or manifest' = 1171 passed, 6 skipped). Complexity ratchet: new=0 increased=0. Next: commit with rebar-ticket trailer + DCO, push to gerrit for LLM-Review + Verified.","timestamp":1787553245449826001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed the fix to Gerrit for review: change 2178 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2178), commit 591861de71ce, Change-Id If5d6646e50015eda0fc3857e581de4b4ac2473a5, trailer rebar-ticket: 39a2-4832-e436-4850. Local gates green (make lint, make typecheck, 519 snapshot/fetch/materialize tests + 39 targeted). Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before Submit; will not self-approve or force.","timestamp":1787554319846044001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787542691850644001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a16d2c90-eebb-4d73-b3ec-02bfd8588f92","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4000-2df3-398d-44e2"},{"link_uuid":"26259122-3a5c-4401-a079-71d5b85c5c9a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"de55-1b7a-543a-4354"},{"link_uuid":"e36cc887-23e0-4eb7-ba6f-46550795c4d9","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"6d56-8c12-9953-4d25"},{"link_uuid":"e05de1f7-ec56-469a-8b03-cf24ee142862","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c6bd-b10e-74f1-407f"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nA normal post-merge `review-plan` from the project checkout made zero LLM calls and took 512.139s before failing because `git fetch origin` hit the 300s timeout. The checkout is partial/promisor (`blob:none`) and its `origin.fetch` maps every remote head. Attested ref resolution calls `fetch_origin()` without a ref, which executes `git fetch --quiet --no-filter origin`; this can traverse/materialize the enormous tickets history while only a code SHA is needed. The failed attempt left partial packs, including one approximately 153.6 MB.\n\nA normal retry from a temporary clone whose origin fetch refspec was main-only crossed the fetch boundary and completed the same review with signed PASS. This discriminates broad-ref transfer from model latency. It is distinct from `strained-bare-turnstone`, which addressed intermittent transport stalls and durable voting behavior, and from `grassy-cracked-morpho`, which covers completion close history-times-tracker scanning.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce attested resolution from a partial/promisor checkout whose origin fetch refspec includes both code and the large tickets branch.\n- Change snapshot ref materialization to fetch only the requested code ref/object while preserving fail-closed attestation semantics and support for remote refs.\n- Preserve blob materialization when the requested snapshot requires it without broadening the remote refspec.\n- Add a regression test that records the exact fetch argv/refspec and rejects an unscoped no-filter origin fetch.\n- Measure the fetch boundary before and after with a representative main-only target.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Resolving a specific attested code ref does not fetch unrelated origin heads.\n- [x] Blobless/promisor checkouts can still materialize the requested snapshot when required.\n- [x] Missing or unreachable requested refs continue to fail closed.\n- [x] Tests pin scoped fetch arguments and cover a checkout with an unrelated large branch.\n- [x] Before/after fetch duration and transferred-object evidence are recorded.\n- [x] No LLM, gate, or tracker behavior is bypassed.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","reason":"Pass the specific ref/object required by attested snapshot materialization into the fetch seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py","reason":"Scope the network fetch to the requested target without fetching unrelated remote heads."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_snapshot_targeted_fetch.py","reason":"Pin scoped fetch argv and fail-closed behavior in partial/promisor repositories."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","c6bd-b10e-74f1-407f"],["relates_to","de55-1b7a-543a-4354"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"df0db9fd-445b-47b2-9b49-0aee0512c128","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["performance","plan-review","git","snapshot"],"ticket_id":"39a2-4832-e436-4850","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Attested ref materialization broad-fetches all origin heads","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["11e91cee-c170-4b10-b7b2-52646620ca62","98b78402-d25e-4916-975c-e92d5bbae7df","31f5afa7-83ad-4528-ba62-7ff850c0af6b","440c4bbd-28d0-4e92-aa2a-2c99a34b9fe7","4f28d006-cf8d-4331-9c22-4c4278796112","b3c48747-b4f1-4c0d-858e-c0cec58e140d","26259122-3a5c-4401-a079-71d5b85c5c9a","df0db9fd-445b-47b2-9b49-0aee0512c128","75de2f27-983a-44fe-a393-984e187e76cb","e36cc887-23e0-4eb7-ba6f-46550795c4d9","e05de1f7-ec56-469a-8b03-cf24ee142862"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787564351842042001,"uuid":"ac2b1706-ba13-43e7-ab12-a874720c74b1"}